# ECHO

TypeScript Expo game. Read `AGENTS.md` before changing gameplay, rendering, or release docs. Read `.claude/skills/echo-gameplay-engine/SKILL.md`, `echo-mobile-visuals`, or `echo-quality-gates` when the change touches that area. Skills are docs, not runtime dependencies.

- Keep collision, history, and scoring in pure TypeScript under `src/game`. Echoes replay recorded samples only. Trails are not lethal.
- Do not call React setState on every simulation tick.
- Do not add login, networking, ads, or notification permission.
- Run `npm test`, `npm run typecheck`, and `npm run lint` after gameplay changes. Do not claim device performance that was not measured.
